{#
  The site's status vocabulary, in one place (design.md §7.4 companion).

  Status badges are the densest visual vocabulary on the site (~250 of
  them) and used to be drawn in three concurrent Bootstrap generations
  (bg-*, bg-*-subtle, text-bg-*) with the same business state coloured
  four different ways across pages — « En attente » was blue here, orange
  there. A colour code nobody can learn protects nothing. One severity →
  one colour, everywhere:

      pending / waiting / scheduled  → warning  (amber: needs someone)
      active / confirmed / done      → success  (green: all is well)
      refused / failed / blocked     → danger   (red: went wrong)
      closed / inactive / neutral    → secondary (grey: nothing to do)
      draft / info                   → info     (teal: informational)

  Usage:
  {% include 'partials/status_badge.html.twig' with {
      status: 'pending',            -- semantic key, table below
      label: "En attente d'examen", -- the words, domain-specific
  } only %}

  `status` accepts the exact keys listed in _tones below; anything else
  renders secondary — an unknown state is a grey fact, never a silent
  green. text-bg-* (Bootstrap 5.3) guarantees the text contrast on every
  tone, which neither bg-* nor bg-*-subtle did.
#}
{% set _tones = {
    'pending': 'warning', 'waiting': 'warning', 'scheduled': 'warning', 'in_progress': 'warning',
    'active': 'success', 'confirmed': 'success', 'accepted': 'success', 'done': 'success', 'success': 'success', 'encoded': 'success',
    'refused': 'danger', 'failed': 'danger', 'error': 'danger', 'blocked': 'danger', 'expired': 'danger',
    'closed': 'secondary', 'inactive': 'secondary', 'cancelled': 'secondary', 'withdrawn': 'secondary', 'archived': 'secondary', 'neutral': 'secondary',
    'draft': 'info', 'info': 'info',
} %}
<span class="badge text-bg-{{ _tones[status|default('neutral')]|default('secondary') }}">{{ label }}</span>
